## Model card

- **Name:** Grok Build 0.1
- **Short description:** xAI’s Grok Build 0.1 is a fast coding-oriented beta model for agentic software engineering and MCP/tooling workflows with 256K context and high throughput.
- **Provider / access:** xAI API / OpenCode contexts per local metadata (`opencode/grok-build-0.1`, `noFreeId`).
- **Release / knowledge:** xAI developer docs reviewed 2026-11-10. Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed source.
- **IDs:** `grok-build-0.1`, `grok-code-fast-1`, `grok-code-fast`, `grok-code-fast-1-0825` (aliases listed in docs).
- **Context window:** 256,000 tokens total (230,400 max output per local metadata).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output (docs state text, image → text).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** $1.00/$2.00 per 1M in/out (<200K), cached $0.20; 2x rates at/above 200K prompt tokens (docs/metadata).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary xAI coding model. Architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SELF-EXCLUSION: I reviewed xAI’s official developer documentation page for `grok-build-0.1`, which provides model capabilities, pricing, rate limits, and regions but does not publish standardized benchmark scores for this exact model. Local metadata references Terminal-Bench 2.1 52.06% and GPQA 89.5% (AA 0616) and notes that a circulated 70.8% SWE-bench Verified figure is inherited/misattributed; I could not independently verify benchmark numerics for this exact model from reviewed official docs in this pass. To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file is saved as `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

